st and they're  passing it on to the consumer now that's  how business works is if my costs go up  i still need to be able to make a profit  and this isn't some sort of high margin  business it's actually a razor thin  margin business and so our good friend  bobby goodlatte he had a nice little  response to senator warren he said those  evil grocers and their checks notes 1.75  profit margins literally  if inflation  of  if inflation goes up seven percent or so  then the entire profit margin of the  grocery store if they do not increase  their prices disappears they begin to  lose money is that what the politicians  are advocating for is for our private  businesses to intentionally lose money  that doesn't make a lot of sense  on top of that food both in the home and  outside the home are up four or five  percent year over year so it's not just  the grocery stores it's also restaurants  and other places where we consume food  everywhere things are getting more  expensive and so if grocery stores do  not increase their prices they won't be  able to pay their employees they won't  be able to actually supply food to their  local communities because they'll be out  of business but of course people who  have never run a business before don't  understand this and so if you don't  believe bobby or me let's just go look  at the actual profit margins fact check  kroger's operating margin for the first  nine months of this year  was 2.4  which was less than the 2.9 a year ago  kroger's making less money on a profit  margin basis so not only are they not  price gouging not only are they not  paying lavish bonuses and making all  this corporate profit  kroger's making less money in 2021 than  they were in 2020. this is complete  nonsense  and the politicians know it but that's  not it if you go ahead and you actually  look and dig a little bit deeper what  you can see here is that it's very clear  they're making less money even though  the grocery stores are actually  increasin